---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const siteTitle = "How to Connect Playwright to Remote Cloud Browsers via connectOverCDP • BrowserReviews";
const siteDescription = "Step-by-step tutorial for connecting Playwright (Python and TypeScript) to remote cloud browsers like 2Captcha Browser API via chromium.connectOverCDP with proxy rotation.";

const schemaMarkup = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Connect Playwright to a Remote Cloud Browser via connectOverCDP",
  "description": "Learn how to establish remote Chrome DevTools Protocol sessions with Playwright using chromium.connectOverCDP, handling CAPTCHAs and stealth bypass.",
  "totalTime": "PT7M",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Prepare the WebSocket Endpoint",
      "text": "Retrieve your 2Captcha API key and configure the remote WebSocket URL with session flags."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Call chromium.connectOverCDP()",
      "text": "Connect Playwright to the remote browser fleet via chromium.connectOverCDP(endpointURL)."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Open a Browser Context and Page",
      "text": "Use standard Playwright context and page APIs with full access to network routing and screenshots."
    }
  ]
};

const tsCode = `import { chromium } from 'playwright';

const API_KEY = process.env.TWOCAPTCHA_API_KEY || 'YOUR_2CAPTCHA_KEY';
const cdpUrl = \`wss://browser.2captcha.com/connect?apiKey=\${API_KEY}&autoSolve=true\`;

async function run() {
  console.log('Connecting Playwright to 2Captcha Browser...');
  const browser = await chromium.connectOverCDP(cdpUrl);

  try {
    const context = browser.contexts()[0] || await browser.newContext();
    const page = await context.newPage();

    console.log('Visiting target ecommerce site...');
    await page.goto('https://nowsecure.nl', { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });

    // Wait for the anti-bot challenge to be cleared automatically
    await page.waitForTimeout(4000);

    const title = await page.title();
    console.log('Successfully loaded page:', title);

    await page.screenshot({ path: 'playwright-result.png' });
  } finally {
    await browser.close();
  }
}

run().catch(console.error);`;

const pythonCode = `import os
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

API_KEY = os.getenv("TWOCAPTCHA_API_KEY", "YOUR_2CAPTCHA_KEY")
cdp_url = f"wss://browser.2captcha.com/connect?apiKey={API_KEY}&autoSolve=true"

with sync_playwright() as p:
    print("Connecting to 2Captcha Cloud Browser...")
    browser = p.chromium.connect_over_cdp(cdp_url)
    
    context = browser.contexts[0] if browser.contexts else browser.new_context()
    page = context.new_page()
    
    page.goto("https://nowsecure.nl")
    page.wait_for_timeout(3000)
    
    print(f"Page Title: {page.title()}")
    page.screenshot(path="python_scraped.png")
    
    browser.close()
    print("Session closed successfully.")`;
---

<Base title={siteTitle} description={siteDescription}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schemaMarkup)} />

  <article class="article-container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> <a href="/guides/">Guides</a> <span>/</span> <span>Playwright Cloud Browser Guide</span>
    </div>

    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span class="badge-tag">Playwright / Python & TS</span>
        <span class="read-time">7 min read • Updated for 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="article-title">How to Connect Playwright to Remote Cloud Browsers via connectOverCDP</h1>
      <p class="article-lead">
        Playwright has become the gold standard for high-performance browser automation and AI agent control. Discover how to connect Playwright to remote cloud browsers to unlock unblockable residential IPs and automatic CAPTCHA solving.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="callout callout-gold">
      <div class="callout-badge">#1 Recommended Playwright Cloud Backend</div>
      <h3>2Captcha Browser API</h3>
      <p>
        Full Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) support with Playwright in Python, TypeScript, and C#. Built-in Cloudflare Turnstile, reCAPTCHA v2/v3, and DataDome solvers, starting at $0.15/hour with zero monthly subscription commitments.
      </p>
      <div class="callout-actions">
        <a href="https://2captcha.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" data-provider="2captcha-browser-api" data-click-location="guide_callout">Get 2Captcha API Key →</a>
        <a href="/reviews/2captcha-browser-api/" class="btn btn-outline">Read Full Review</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="article-content">
      <h2>Why Playwright `connectOverCDP`?</h2>
      <p>
        Playwright provides a dedicated method called <code>chromium.connectOverCDP(endpointURL)</code> specifically designed for connecting to remote Chrome instances over WebSocket. This approach offers several massive advantages over local browser execution:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Zero Chromium Downloads in CI/CD:</strong> Your Docker images and GitHub Actions don't need to install 400MB of browser binaries or OS dependencies.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatic Fingerprint Spoofing:</strong> Cloud browsers inject realistic canvas, WebGL, WebRTC, and hardware concurrency fingerprints to prevent bot detection.</li>
        <li><strong>Built-in Residential Proxies:</strong> Every request is routed through verified residential IPs across 220+ countries.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>TypeScript / Node.js Implementation</h2>
      <div class="code-container">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span>playwright-2captcha.ts</span>
          <span class="code-lang">TypeScript</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>{tsCode}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Python Implementation</h2>
      <p>
        For data science and Python scraping teams, the setup in <code>playwright.sync_api</code> or <code>async_api</code> is equally simple:
      </p>
      <div class="code-container">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span>scraper.py</span>
          <span class="code-lang">Python</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>{pythonCode}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Comparison: Playwright on Local Server vs 2Captcha Browser API</h2>
      <table class="spec-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Feature</th>
            <th>Local Playwright</th>
            <th>2Captcha Browser API (#1)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>RAM Usage per Thread</strong></td>
            <td>250MB–450MB on host</td>
            <td>0MB (Cloud offloaded)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile Bypass</strong></td>
            <td>Fails / Blocked</td>
            <td>100% Native Automated</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Residential Proxy Rotation</strong></td>
            <td>Requires external config</td>
            <td>Built-in (220+ Countries)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Cost Model</strong></td>
            <td>Server hosting costs</td>
            <td>$0.15/hour (Pay-As-You-Go)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="next-step-box">
        <h3>Explore AI Agent Browser Tools</h3>
        <p>
          Need to give your AI assistants (Claude, Cursor, LangChain) the same browsing capabilities? Check out our review of the <strong>2Captcha Browser MCP</strong> server.
        </p>
        <div class="next-step-links">
          <a href="/mcp/2captcha-browser-mcp/" class="btn btn-outline">Read 2Captcha Browser MCP Review</a>
          <a href="/calculator" class="btn btn-outline">Calculate Compute Costs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

